From: Ubuntu Rockchip Builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkvdec: allow image-format controls in requests

Stateless codec clients submit the sequence header with every request, so
the first one necessarily arrives after CAPTURE buffers have been
allocated.  rkvdec_s_ctrl() rejected any such control with -EBUSY whenever
the codec-derived image format had not been latched yet, which breaks the
normal GStreamer request flow and prevents a VA-API bridge from supplying
its first H.264 SPS atomically with the frame.

Narrow the check instead of dropping it.  The queue must still be refused
when the new image format needs a different capture format: rkvdec can
select NV12, NV15, NV16 or NV20 depending on bit depth and chroma format,
and NV20 needs two and a half times the NV12 buffer size, so applying such
a change to buffers already handed to the hardware would have the decoder
write past them.  Comparing the resulting fourcc lets the harmless
ANY-to-8-bit transition through while keeping that protection.

Signed-off-by: Ubuntu Rockchip Builder <builder@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 104b4a142..a139e8135 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -183,9 +183,22 @@ static int rkvdec_s_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 
 	image_fmt = desc->ops->get_image_fmt(ctx, ctrl);
 	if (rkvdec_image_fmt_changed(ctx, image_fmt)) {
+		u32 fourcc = rkvdec_enum_decoded_fmt(ctx, 0, image_fmt);
+
+		/*
+		 * A stateless client submits the sequence header with every
+		 * request, so the first one necessarily arrives once CAPTURE
+		 * buffers are already allocated; refusing all of them breaks
+		 * the normal request flow. Only refuse when the new image
+		 * format needs a different capture format, which is exactly
+		 * the case where the buffers already handed to the hardware
+		 * are the wrong size and letting the decoder proceed would
+		 * have it write past them.
+		 */
 		vq = v4l2_m2m_get_vq(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx,
 				     V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE);
-		if (vb2_is_busy(vq))
+		if (vb2_is_busy(vq) &&
+		    fourcc != ctx->decoded_fmt.fmt.pix_mp.pixelformat)
 			return -EBUSY;
 
 		ctx->image_fmt = image_fmt;
